tags: event

= Wittorf Affair

An associate and close personal friend of Ernst Thälmann, John Wittorf, is accused of embezzling campaign funds, diverting thousands of Reichsmarks for personal use, and Thälmann is accused of covering up the affair. The party's central committee considers this charge serious.

The information has already leaked to the press and the party's leadership is infuriated by Thälmann's coverup.

What should we do?

- @expel_thalmann
- @broke_lmao
- @secret

@expel_thalmann
title: Expel Thälmann and the others from their positions, corruption will not be tolerated.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: If the party have no resources, what could Wittorf have embezzled?
on-arrival: n_advisors -= 1 if thalmann_advisor = 1; thalmann_advisor = 0; workers_kpd -= 4; unemployed_kpd -= 4

Thälmann and other implicated officials are expelled from their positions. The Comintern, and Stalin in particular, are carefully watching us.

@broke_lmao
title: Embezzle what?! We have no money...
view-if: resources <= 0
on-arrival: conciliator_dissent += 5; marxist_leninist_dissent += 5

Upon closer inspection, it is discovered that Wittorf could not have embezzeled that much money because the party didn't have it in the first place. The people who made these false accusations are penalized accordingly, and Thälmann is found innocent.

@secret
title: The press... hasn't published anything?
view-if: spd_relation >=30
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: They can't publish anything if we have no money to embezzle, genius...
on-arrival: wittorf_secret = 1; n_advisors -= 1 if thalmann_advisor = 1; thalmann_advisor = 0;

For whatever reason, the SPD and Leninbund have not published anything about the scandal. This leaves the conflict as a purely internal matter, away from the eyes of workers.